  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MSI Reproductive Choices - ASPIRE project support 2024-2028 - MSI Reproductive Choices - ASPIRE project support 2024-2028, 202403-2028</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">MSI Reproductive Choices - ASPIRE projektst&#xf6;d 2024-2028</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Marie Stopes International har inkommit med en projektans&#xf6;kan, om 75 MSEK under perioden 2024-2028, f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra ASPIRE projektet i Zambia. ASPIRE syftar till att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra tillg&#xe5;ngen och utnyttjandet av h&#xe4;lsov&#xe5;rdstj&#xe4;nster inom ramen f&#xf6;r sexuell och reproduktiv h&#xe4;lsa. Projektet kommer att n&#xe5; kvinnor, m&#xe4;n och ungdomar med h&#xf6;gkvalitativa, r&#xe4;ttighetsbaserade och klientcentrerade tj&#xe4;nster inom sexuell och reproduktiv h&#xe4;lsa, f&#xf6;r att f&#xf6;rhindra o&#xf6;nskade graviditeter, os&#xe4;kra aborter och i slut&#xe4;ndan minska antalet d&#xf6;dsfall bland m&#xf6;drar.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Marie Stopes International has submitted a project application for SEK 75 million during the period 2024-2028, to implement the ASPIRE project in Zambia. ASPIRE aims to improve access to -/and utilization of health services in particular SRHR services. The project will reach women, men and adolescents with high-quality, rights-based and client-centered sexual and reproductive health services to prevent unwanted pregnancies, unsafe abortions and ultimately reduce maternal deaths.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal of ASPIRE to contribute to reduced maternal mortality and morbidity and to improve womens health. 

The project will reach women, men and adolescents with high-quality rights-based and client-centred sexual and reproductive health services, to avert unintended pregnancies, unsafe abortions and ultimately reduce the number of maternal deaths.</narrative>
  </description>
